<usx version="3.0"><chapter number="5" style="c" altnumber="5a" sid=" 5" /><char style="ca">5b</char> Stray text on the chapter line after a second ca, before any paragraph.<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="" />Chapter 5 holds deliberately damaged USFM that can still exist at rest in a Paratext 9 project. A nameless marker follows this sentence. <verse eid="" /></para><para style="" status="unknown">2 <verse number="2" style="v" sid="" />A bare backslash after a character marker <char style="bd" closed="false" /><verse eid="" /></para><para style="" status="unknown">text after it. <verse number="3" style="v" sid="" />A bare backslash at the end of a verse </para><para style="" status="unknown" vid="" /><para style="b" vid="">Stray text after a blank-line marker.<verse eid="" /></para><chapter eid=" 5" /></usx>